From 154efe6166fba12e19b19b2931fafd00aaf9577b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 20:26:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/6] fix(post): refuse a canned cycle with no feed and a
 Tormach cut with the spindle stopped

A canned cycle whose FeedRate is missing or not positive is refused by
name in every post that writes the cycle's own F (tormach, fanuc, haas,
sinumerik, mazak, doosan-dnm, grblhal, fanuc-lathe); heidenhain no
longer falls back to the last modal feed. tormach.cps also refuses a
feed, arc or cycle with the spindle stopped (no S.. M3 since the last
M5), a touch probe's 0 rpm section exempt.

The Tormach mill goldens are now runnable 770MX programs, posted from
the legacy streams dressed with setup/operation/tool records, a tool
change, a spindle speed and each cycle's chain feed
(tests/common/legacy_program.rs); every other dialect's drill and tap
goldens gain the cycle's F. The other spindle mill posts take the
spindle rule in #1359.

Fixes #1357

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
