From 8be70713079859afdd03bb9d658bb808e560db8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:42:20 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] fix(post): refuse a cut with the spindle stopped in every
 spindle mill dialect

The spindle-state rule #1357 gave tormach.cps (with the #1367 review's
touch-probe fix) is ported to fanuc, haas, sinumerik, mazak, heidenhain,
doosan-dnm, grblhal, tinyg and carvera. Each tracks the spindle from its
preamble start (S.. M3; MOTON S..; M3 S..) to the next stop, and refuses
a feed, arc or canned cycle with it stopped, by name, posting nothing
for it. A touch-probe section (0 rpm on a PARAM ToolKind touch probe) is
exempt; a cutter at 0 rpm is not. Heidenhain checks its native cycle
after the tapping refusals, so those keep their own names.

Every mill dialect's conformance golden is now posted from as_program
(tool change, spindle speed, op comments), and the moved goldens are
regenerated: lines are only added (setup/operation/tool comments, the
tool change, the spindle start; Heidenhain and Sinumerik renumber).
Heidenhain's tap_plate, refused before only for want of a spindle
speed, now posts and has a golden. Fixture streams in the post crate's
tests and in fourth_axis_pose / tinyg_post state a spindle speed.

Pinned by post_spindle_rule_all.rs (feed, arc, hole, 0-rpm cutter vs
touch probe, section after the stop, per dialect).

Fixes #1359

